#### Variation 3: Federated Shared Context (Module-Provided Context)

**Standard Shared Context**: Shell owns and provides all shared contexts

**Variation**: Modules can provide their own contexts for other modules to consume:

```typescript
// Notifications MFE exports context
export const NotificationContext = createContext<NotificationState>(null);

// Shell imports and re-exports
import { NotificationContext } from 'notificationsMfe/context';

export function Shell() {
  return (
    <NotificationContext.Provider value={notificationState}>
      <ClaimsMfe />
      <ProviderMfe />
    </NotificationContext.Provider>
  );
}
```

**Use When**: Domain-specific contexts owned by specialized modules (e.g., notification system, analytics)

